WHERE: 
Where is used to filter the rows based on a condition before grouping and
aggregation are performed.

(1) Execute before GroupBy
(2) Cannot use aggregate1 functions such as: SUM(), AVG(), MIN(), MAX(), COUNT().

Eg:
Select * from TableName
Where columnName > 200;


HAVING:
HAVING is sued to filter groups after grouping and aggregate function are p1erformed.
(1) Executes after GroupBy
(2) Can use Aggregate functions.

Eg:
Select DepartmentID , Count(*)
From Employees
Group By DepartmentID
Having Count(*) > 5;